ma 4D (beta)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"publish from houdini (beta)\" href=\"/docs/guides/publish-from-houdini\" id=\"lnk-publish-from-houdini-beta-2\">Publish from Houdini (beta)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"publish from solidworks (beta)\" href=\"/docs/guides/publish-from-solidworks\" id=\"lnk-publish-from-solidworks-beta-2\">Publish from SolidWorks (beta)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"publish from spline, and figma (beta)\" href=\"/docs/guides/publish-from-spline\" id=\"lnk-publish-from-spline-and-figma-beta-2\">Publish from Spline, and Figma (beta)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"camera paths and default walkthroughs\" href=\"/docs/guides/camera-paths\" id=\"lnk-camera-paths-and-default-walkthroughs-2\">Camera paths and default walkthroughs</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"hotspots and doors\" href=\"/docs/guides/hotspots-and-doors\" id=\"lnk-hotspots-and-doors-2\">Hotspots and doors</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse capture: film a room (beta)\" href=\"/docs/guides/film-a-room\" id=\"lnk-verse-capture-film-a-room-beta-2\">Verse Capture: film a room (beta)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse play: host a web game\" href=\"/docs/guides/host-a-web-game\" id=\"lnk-verse-play-host-a-web-game-2\">Verse Play: host a web game</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"spatial bench\" href=\"/docs/guides/spatial-bench\" id=\"lnk-spatial-bench-2\">Spatial Bench</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"light and dark theme\" href=\"/docs/guides/light-and-dark-theme\" id=\"lnk-light-and-dark-theme-2\">Light and dark theme</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"share privately with tokens\" href=\"/docs/guides/share-privately\" id=\"lnk-share-privately-with-tokens-2\">Share privately with tokens</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"show your clients who looked\" href=\"/docs/guides/analytics\" id=\"lnk-show-your-clients-who-looked-2\">Show your clients who looked</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed anywhere: wordpress, shopify, webflow\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-anywhere\" id=\"lnk-embed-anywhere-wordpress-shopify-webflow-2\">Embed anywhere: WordPress, Shopify, Webflow</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse for commerce: 3d on product pages (woocommerce, magento, bigcommerce, salesforce)\" href=\"/docs/guides/commerce\" id=\"lnk-verse-for-commerce-3d-on-product-pages-w-2\">Verse for Commerce: 3D on product pages (WooCommerce, Magento, BigCommerce, Salesforce)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse links and embeds: embed the viewer\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-the-viewer\" id=\"lnk-verse-links-and-embeds-embed-the-viewer-2\">Verse links and embeds: embed the viewer</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"export a flythrough video\" href=\"/docs/guides/export-video\" id=\"lnk-export-a-flythrough-video-2\">Export a flythrough video</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"collect client review comments\" href=\"/docs/guides/collect-review-comments\" id=\"lnk-collect-client-review-comments-2\">Collect client review comments</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"author a guided tour\" href=\"/docs/guides/author-a-guided-tour\" id=\"lnk-author-a-guided-tour-2\">Author a guided tour</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"video on surfaces, sound in the room\" href=\"/docs/guides/video-and-audio\" id=\"lnk-video-on-surfaces-sound-in-the-room-2\">Video on surfaces, sound in the room</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"publish from ifc or usd\" href=\"/docs/guides/publish-from-ifc\" id=\"lnk-publish-from-ifc-or-usd-2\">Publish from IFC or USD</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"upload fbx and obj\" href=\"/docs/guides/upload-fbx-obj\" id=\"lnk-upload-fbx-and-obj-2\">Upload FBX and OBJ</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"build a configurator\" href=\"/docs/guides/build-a-configurator\" id=\"lnk-build-a-configurator-2\">Build a configurator</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"present a scene to a room\" href=\"/docs/guides/present-a-scene\" id=\"lnk-present-a-scene-to-a-room-2\">Present a scene to a room</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse-prepare: the local compression step\" href=\"/docs/guides/verse-prepare\" id=\"lnk-verse-prepare-the-local-compression-step-2\">verse-prepare: the local compression step</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"tune quality knobs\" href=\"/docs/guides/tune-quality\" id=\"lnk-tune-quality-knobs-2\">Tune quality knobs</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"run your own server\" href=\"/docs/guides/run-your-own-server\" id=\"lnk-run-your-own-server-2\">Run your own server</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"monitor production\" href=\"/docs/guides/monitor-production\" id=\"lnk-monitor-production-2\">Monitor production</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"ask verse, the site assistant\" href=\"/docs/guides/ask-verse\" id=\"lnk-ask-verse-the-site-assistant-2\">Ask Verse, the site assistant</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse home: floor plan to 3d home\" href=\"/docs/guides/floor-plan-to-3d\" id=\"lnk-verse-home-floor-plan-to-3d-home-2\">Verse Home: floor plan to 3D home</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse home: plan to a home buyers walk, restyle and tour\" href=\"/docs/guides/instant-home\" id=\"lnk-verse-home-plan-to-a-home-buyers-walk-re-2\">Verse Home: plan to a home buyers walk, restyle and tour</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"&lt;verse-viewer&gt;: one tag, any page\" href=\"/docs/guides/web-component\" id=\"lnk-one-tag-any-page-2\">&lt;verse-viewer&gt;: one tag, any page</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"designer tools: framer, webflow, figma\" href=\"/docs/guides/designer-tools\" id=\"lnk-designer-tools-framer-webflow-figma-2\">Designer tools: Framer, Webflow, Figma</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"react and vue wrappers\" href=\"/docs/guides/react-and-vue\" id=\"lnk-react-and-vue-wrappers-2\">React and Vue wrappers</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"rest client round trip\" href=\"/docs/guides/rest-client\" aria-current=\"page\" id=\"lnk-rest-client-round-trip-2\">REST client round trip</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"sell with woocommerce\" href=\"/docs/guides/sell-with-woocommerce\" id=\"lnk-sell-with-woocommerce-2\">Sell with WooCommerce</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"sell with bigcommerce\" href=\"/docs/guides/sell-with-bigcommerce\" id=\"lnk-sell-with-bigcommerce-2\">Sell with BigCommerce</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"sell with magento / adobe commerce\" href=\"/docs/guides/sell-with-magento\" id=\"lnk-sell-with-magento-adobe-commerce-2\">Sell with Magento / Adobe Commerce</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed in wix\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-in-wix\" id=\"lnk-embed-in-wix-2\">Embed in Wix</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed in squarespace\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-in-squarespace\" id=\"lnk-embed-in-squarespace-2\">Embed in Squarespace</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed in framer\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-in-framer\" id=\"lnk-embed-in-framer-2\">Embed in Framer</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed in ghost and hubspot\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-in-ghost-and-hubspot\" id=\"lnk-embed-in-ghost-and-hubspot-2\">Embed in Ghost and HubSpot</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"automate with zapier\" href=\"/docs/guides/automate-with-zapier\" id=\"lnk-automate-with-zapier-2\">Automate with Zapier</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"automate with make\" href=\"/docs/guides/automate-with-make\" id=\"lnk-automate-with-make-2\">Automate with Make</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"automate with n8n\" href=\"/docs/guides/automate-with-n8n\" id=\"lnk-automate-with-n8n-2\">Automate with n8n</a></section><section id=\"sec-item-10\"><h2>Blog & updates</h2><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"all posts\" href=\"/docs/blog/index\" id=\"lnk-all-posts-2\">All posts</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"how verse streams a building\" href=\"/docs/blog/how-verse-streams-a-building\" id=\"lnk-how-verse-streams-a-building-2\">How Verse streams a building</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"2.7: what's new for you\" href=\"/docs/blog/verse-engine-2-7-whats-new\" id=\"lnk-2-7-what-s-new-for-you-2\">2.7: what's new for you</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"2.0 release notes for humans\" href=\"/docs/blog/2-0-release-notes-for-humans\" id=\"lnk-2-0-release-notes-for-humans-2\">2.0 release notes for humans</a></section><section id=\"sec-item-11\"><h2>Integrations</h2><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"integrations: every platform at a glance\" href=\"/docs/integrations\" id=\"lnk-integrations-every-platform-at-a-glance-2\">Integrations: every platform at a glance</a></section><section id=\"sec-item-12\"><h2>API & SDK</h2><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse api, sdk and mcp: embed, sdk, webhooks\" href=\"/docs/developers\" id=\"lnk-verse-api-sdk-and-mcp-embed-sdk-webhooks-2\">Verse API, SDK and MCP: embed, SDK, webhooks</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse api reference\" href=\"/docs/api\" id=\"lnk-verse-api-reference-2\">Verse API reference</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"api quickstart\" href=\"/docs/api-quickstart\" id=\"lnk-api-quickstart-2\">API quickstart</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"api changelog\" href=\"/docs/api-changelog\" id=\"lnk-api-changelog-2\">API changelog</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed sdk reference\" href=\"/docs/embed-sdk\" id=\"lnk-embed-sdk-reference-2\">Embed SDK reference</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse sdk: js / ts (@ctruhtech/verse-sdk)\" href=\"/docs/sdk\" id=\"lnk-verse-sdk-js-ts-ctruhtech-verse-sdk-2\">Verse SDK: JS / TS (@ctruhtech/verse-sdk)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse mcp server for ai agents\" href=\"/docs/mcp\" id=\"lnk-verse-mcp-server-for-ai-agents-2\">Verse MCP server for AI agents</a></section><p class=\"docs-no-results\" hidden>No matching guides.</p></div></nav></aside><div class=\"doc-body\"><article class=\"doc-article\" id=\"art-doc-article\"><h1 id=\"the-rest-client-round-trip-file-in-link-out-numbers-back\">The REST client round trip: file in, link out, numbers back<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#the-rest-client-round-trip-file-in-link-out-numbers-back\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section\">#</a></h1>\n<p>Everything an integration does with Verse is five calls: get a token, hand over a file (or a URL the server fetches), wait for the compile, make a share link, read the analytics. A webhook replaces the waiting. This guide walks the round trip with <code>@ctruhtech/verse-sdk</code> and with plain <code>curl</code>, so it maps onto any language.</p>\n<p><strong>Status:</strong> tested. The whole round trip runs against a real server in <code>web/test/fix-verify-integrations.mjs</code>: account → <code>publishFromUrl</code> (through a redirect) → done → share link → analytics (JSON and CSV, per scene and per account) → a stranger is refused → webhook created → a real signed <code>scene.ready</code> delivery to a local receiver → the delivery log. The upload-from-URL guard is tested on 13 reserved address families and 14 hostile URLs. The SDK&#39;s own tests: <code>sdk</code>, <code>npm test</code>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"0-pick-a-client\">0. Pick a client<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#0-pick-a-client\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-2\">#</a></h2>\n<ul><li><strong>JavaScript / TypeScript:</strong> <code>npm install @ctruhtech/verse-sdk</code> — typed, dependency-free, Node 18+ and browsers. Reference: <a href=\"/docs/sdk\" id=\"lnk-js-ts-sdk\">JS / TS SDK</a>.</li><li><strong>Anything else:</strong> the API is plain JSON over HTTPS (<a href=\"/docs/api\" id=\"lnk-api-reference\">API reference</a>); the <code>curl</code> lines below are the whole contract. A Postman collection is linked from the API reference.</li></ul>\n<div class=\"doc-code\" data-lang=\"js\"><div><span>Code</span><button type=\"button\" data-copy-local id=\"btn-copy\">Copy ⧉</button></div><pre><code class=\"lang-js\">import { VerseClient, VerseError } from &quot;@ctruhtech/verse-sdk&quot;;\nconst verse = new VerseClient({ baseUrl: &quot;https://verse.ctruh.com&quot;, token: process.env.VERSE_TOKEN });</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"1-a-token\">1. A token<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#1-a-token\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-3\">#</a></h2>\n<p>An account is a token. Create one once, store it like an API key; it is shown once.</p>\n<div class=\"doc-code\" data-lang=\"js\"><div><span>Code</span><button type=\"button\" data-copy-local id=\"btn-copy-2\">Copy ⧉</button></div><pre><code class=\"lang-js\">const { accountId, token } = await new VerseClient({ baseUrl }).createAccount(&quot;Acme Realty&quot;);</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"doc-code\" data-lang=\"sh\"><div><span>Code</span><button type=\"button\" data-copy-local id=\"btn-copy-3\">Copy ⧉</button></div><pre><code class=\"lang-sh\">curl -sS -X POST https://verse.ctruh.com/v1/account -H &quot;Content-Type: application/json&quot; -d &#39;{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Acme Realty&quot;}&#39;\n# {&quot;accountId&quot;:&quot;…&quot;,&quot;token&quot;:&quot;&lt;64 hex, shown once&gt;&quot;}</code></pre></div>\n<p>Every call below sends it as <code>Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN</code>. Whatever you upload with it, the account owns. Self-hosted servers in keyed mode take <code>X-API-Key</code> instead (<a href=\"/docs/api#authentication\" id=\"lnk-authentication\">Authentication</a>).</p>\n<h2 id=\"2-the-file-in\">2. The file in<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#2-the-file-in\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-4\">#</a></h2>\n<p>Two ways. A <strong>body upload</strong> when the bytes are with you:</p>\n<div class=\"doc-code\" data-lang=\"js\"><div><span>Code</span><button type=\"button\" data-copy-local id=\"btn-copy-4\">Copy ⧉</button></div><pre><code class=\"lang-js\">const { job } = await verse.upload(readFileSync(&quot;villa.glb&quot;), { name: &quot;palm-villa&quot; });</code></pre></div>\n<p>An <strong>upload from URL</strong> when the file already has one — a Dropbox or Drive share link, a presigned S3 / R2 / GCS URL, a CMS media library. The server fetches it itself, so the bytes never pass through your process or an automation platform:</p>\n<div class=\"doc-code\" data-lang=\"js\"><div><span>Code</span><button type=\"button\" data-copy-local id=\"btn-copy-5\">Copy ⧉</button></div><pre><code class=\"lang-js\">const { job, sizeBytes, source } = await verse.uploadFromUrl(&quot;https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/…/villa.glb?dl=1&quot;, { name: &quot;palm-villa&quot; });</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"doc-code\" data-lang=\"sh\"><div><span>Code</span><button type=\"button\" data-copy-local id=\"btn-copy-6\">Copy ⧉</button></div><pre><code class=\"lang-sh\">curl -sS -X POST https://verse.ctruh.com/v1/ingest/url -H &quot;Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN&quot; -H &quot;Content-Type: application/json&quot; \\\n  -d &#39;{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/…/villa.glb?dl=1&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;palm-villa&quot;}&#39;\n# HTTP/1.1 202 Accepted   {&quot;job&quot;:&quot;palm-villa-3f1c9a2b7e04&quot;,&quot;sizeBytes&quot;:48213990,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;uc1234.dl.dropboxusercontent.com&quot;}</code></pre></div>\n<p>Body fields: <code>url</code> (required, absolute <code>http(s)</code>), <code>name</code>, <code>kind</code> (<code>ifc</code>, <code>usd</code>, … when the extension does not say), <code>bake</code>, <code>path</code>, <code>look</code>, <code>scan</code> — the same knobs as a body upload. Dropbox links need <code>dl=1</code>; Drive links need &quot;Anyone with the link&quot;.</p>\n<p>What the server will <strong>not</strong> fetch, and answers <code>400 url_blocked</code> to: anything but <code>http(s)</code>, a URL with credentials, and any host that resolves to a private, loopback, link-local, cloud-metadata, CGNAT or multicast address (IPv6 ULA, link-local and v4-mapped alike). Redirects are followed by hand, at most three, each re-vetted. The download is streamed to disk and cut at the upload limit (<code>413 file_too_large</code>; a <code>Content-Length</code> over it is refused before a byte is read). An empty file is <code>400 empty_file</code>, a 404 at the URL is <code>404 url_fetch_failed</code>, a redirect loop or a timeout is <code>502</code> / <code>504 url_fetch_failed</code>. Full table: <a href=\"/docs/api#upload-from-url\" id=\"lnk-upload-from-url\">Upload from URL</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"3-wait-for-the-compile\">3. Wait for the compile<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#3-wait-for-the-compile\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-5\">#</a></h2>\n<div class=\"doc-code\" data-lang=\"js\"><div><span>Code</span><button type=\"button\" data-copy-local id=\"btn-copy-7\">Copy ⧉</button></div><pre><code class=\"lang-js\">const rec = await verse.waitForJob(job, { onStage: (stage, r) =&gt; console.log(stage, r.etaText ?? &quot;&quot;) });\n// rec.status === &quot;done&quot;, rec.url === &quot;https://verse.ctruh.com/?vpk=ingest/palm-villa-3f1c9a2b7e04.vpk&quot;</code></pre></div>\n<p><code>publishFromUrl(url, opts)</code> (and <code>publish(bytes, opts)</code>) is the upload and the wait in one call. With <code>curl</code>, poll <code>GET /v1/ingest/&lt;job&gt;</code> every few seconds until <code>status</code> is <code>done</code> or <code>error</code>; the record carries <code>stage</code>, <code>etaText</code> and, on failure, a friendly <code>errorInfo</code> (<a href=\"/docs/api#get-v1-ingest-job\" id=\"lnk-the-job-record\">the job record</a>).</p>\n<p>Or do not poll at all: section 6.</p>\n<h2 id=\"4-a-link\">4. A link<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#4-a-link\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-6\">#</a></h2>\n<p>The record&#39;s <code>url</code> opens the scene. For a client, make a <strong>share link</strong>: a private scene stays private, and the link can be revoked.</p>\n<div class=\"doc-code\" data-lang=\"js\"><div><span>Code</span><button type=\"button\" data-copy-local id=\"btn-copy-8\">Copy ⧉</button></div><pre><code class=\"lang-js\">const link = await verse.scenes.shares.create(job);\nconst url = verse.shareLink(job, { share: link.shareToken });   // …/view?vpk=ingest/&lt;job&gt;.vpk&amp;share=&lt;token&gt;</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"doc-code\" data-lang=\"sh\"><div><span>Code</span><button type=\"button\" data-copy-local id=\"btn-copy-9\">Copy ⧉</button></div><pre><code class=\"lang-sh\">curl -sS -X POST https://verse.ctruh.com/v1/scenes/$JOB/share -H &quot;Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN&quot;\n# {&quot;shareId&quot;:&quot;…&quot;,&quot;shareToken&quot;:&quot;&lt;32 hex&gt;&quot;,…}</code></pre></div>\n<p><code>shareLink()</code> takes the same knobs as the viewer (<code>look</code>, <code>variant</code>, <code>cfg</code>, <code>view</code>, <code>bg</code>), so one link can open the oak variant from the kitchen. Embedding the link on a page: <a href=\"/docs/guides/web-component\" id=\"lnk-item\"><code>&lt;verse-viewer&gt;</code></a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"5-the-numbers-back\">5. The numbers back<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#5-the-numbers-back\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-7\">#</a></h2>\n<div class=\"doc-code\" data-lang=\"js\"><div><span>Code</span><button type=\"button\" data-copy-local id=\"btn-copy-10\">Copy ⧉</button></div><pre><code class=\"lang-js\">const a = await verse.scenes.analytics(job, { days: 30 });        // views, uniqueViewers, time, funnel, rooms, devices, daily…\nconst csv = await verse.scenes.analyticsCsv(job, { days: 30 });   // the same as CSV text\nconst all = await verse.accountAnalytics({ days: 30 });            // every scene you own, one row each</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"doc-code\" data-lang=\"sh\"><div><span>Code</span><button type=\"button\" data-copy-local id=\"btn-copy-11\">Copy ⧉</button></div><pre><code class=\"lang-sh\">curl -sS &quot;https://verse.ctruh.com/v1/scenes/$JOB/analytics?days=30&quot; -H &quot;Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN&quot;\ncurl -sS &quot;https://verse.ctruh.com/v1/account/analytics.csv?days=30&quot; -H &quot;Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN&quot; -o scenes.csv</code></pre></div>\n<p>Only the owner can read a scene&#39;s analytics; anyone else gets a <code>404</code>, the same answer as for a scene that does not exist. What each field means: <a href=\"/docs/api#analytics\" id=\"lnk-analytics\">Analytics</a> and the guide <a href=\"/docs/guides/analytics\" id=\"lnk-show-your-clients-who-looked-3\">Show your clients who looked</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"6-a-webhook-instead-of-polling\">6. A webhook instead of polling<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#6-a-webhook-instead-of-polling\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-8\">#</a></h2>\n<p>Register a receiver once; the server POSTs to it when a scene finishes (or fails), when a review comment lands, when a version goes live, when a configurator schema changes.</p>\n<div class=\"doc-code\" data-lang=\"js\"><div><span>Code</span><button type=\"button\" data-copy-local id=\"btn-copy-12\">Copy ⧉</button></div><pre><code class=\"lang-js\">const hook = await verse.webhooks.create({ url: &quot;https://example.com/verse-hook&quot;, events: [&quot;scene.ready&quot;, &quot;scene.failed&quot;] });\nsaveSomewhereSafe(hook.secret);                 // shown once; list() only ever shows a hint\nconst { deliveries } = await verse.webhooks.deliveries(hook.id);   // the last 50, newest first, ok / status per try</code></pre></div>\n<p>A delivery is one <code>POST</code> of <code>{ id, event, t, account, data }</code> with <code>X-Verse-Event</code>, <code>X-Verse-Delivery</code>, <code>X-Verse-Timestamp</code> and <code>X-Verse-Signature: sha256=&lt;hex&gt;</code> — HMAC-SHA256 with the secret over <code>&lt;timestamp&gt;.&lt;raw body&gt;</code>. Verify it over the bytes you received, compare in constant time, reject stale timestamps:</p>\n<div class=\"doc-code\" data-lang=\"js\"><div><span>Code</span><button type=\"button\" data-copy-local id=\"btn-copy-13\">Copy ⧉</button></div><pre><code class=\"lang-js\">import { createHmac, timingSafeEqual } from &quot;node:crypto&quot;;\nconst expected = &quot;sha256=&quot; + createHmac(&quot;sha256&quot;, SECRET).update(`${req.headers[&quot;x-verse-timestamp&quot;]}.${rawBody}`).digest(&quot;hex&quot;);\nconst ok = expected.length === sig.length &amp;&amp; timingSafeEqual(Buffer.from(expected), Buffer.from(sig));</code></pre></div>\n<p><code>scene.ready</code>&#39;s <code>data</code> is <code>{ job, status: &quot;done&quot;, url, vpkUrl?, stats? }</code> — enough to make the share link (section 4) without another call. A non-2xx answer or a timeout is retried three times (2 s, then 8 s). All events and payloads: <a href=\"/docs/api#webhooks-2-7\" id=\"lnk-webhooks\">Webhooks</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"7-errors\">7. Errors<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#7-errors\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-9\">#</a></h2>\n<p>Every failure the SDK throws is a <code>VerseError</code> with the API&#39;s error contract decoded: <code>status</code>, <code>code</code> (<code>url_blocked</code>, <code>file_too_large</code>, <code>no_meshes</code>, <code>rate_limited</code>, …), <code>message</code> (safe to show), <code>retryable</code>, and <code>errorInfo</code> with a <code>fix</code> sentence for ingest failures. Transient network failures are retried once; server answers never are.</p>\n<div class=\"doc-code\" data-lang=\"js\"><div><span>Code</span><button type=\"button\" data-copy-local id=\"btn-copy-14\">Copy ⧉</button></div><pre><code class=\"lang-js\">try {\n  await verse.publishFromUrl(url);\n} catch (e) {\n  if (e instanceof VerseError &amp;&amp; e.code === &quot;url_blocked&quot;) console.log(&quot;that link is not public:&quot;, e.message);\n  else throw e;\n}</code></pre></div>\n<p>With <code>curl</code>: the body is <code>{ &quot;error&quot;: &quot;&lt;sentence&gt;&quot;, &quot;errorInfo&quot;: { &quot;code&quot;, &quot;title&quot;, &quot;message&quot;, &quot;fix&quot;, &quot;retryable&quot; } }</code> and the header <code>X-Verse-Error: 1</code> says the Verse server spoke (as opposed to the network edge). <a href=\"/docs/api#error-contract\" id=\"lnk-error-contract\">Error contract</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-same-five-calls-elsewhere\">The same five calls, elsewhere<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#the-same-five-calls-elsewhere\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-10\">#</a></h2>\n<ul><li><strong>No code:</strong> Zapier, Make and n8n apps wrap exactly these calls — <a href=\"/docs/guides/automate-with-zapier\" id=\"lnk-zapier\">Zapier</a>, <a href=\"/docs/guides/automate-with-make\" id=\"lnk-make\">Make</a>, <a href=\"/docs/guides/automate-with-n8n\" id=\"lnk-n8n\">n8n</a>.</li><li><strong>CI:</strong> <code>sdk/examples/</code> has a GitHub Actions workflow that publishes a GLB on push.</li><li><strong>Self-hosted:</strong> replace the origin; the API is the same (<a href=\"/docs/guides/run-your-own-server\" id=\"lnk-run-your-own-server-3\">Run your own server</a>).</li></ul>\n<p>See also: <a href=\"/docs/api\" id=\"lnk-api-reference-2\">API reference</a>, <a href=\"/docs/sdk\" id=\"lnk-js-ts-sdk-2\">JS / TS SDK</a>, <a href=\"/docs/integrations\" id=\"lnk-integrations\">Integrations</a>.</p></article><div class=\"doc-source\">Published documentation from <a href=\"https://verse.ctruh.com/docs/#/guides/rest-client\" id=\"lnk-verse-by-ctruh\">Verse by Ctruh</a></div></div><aside class=\"docs-toc\" id=\"asd-docs-toc\"><p>ON THIS PAGE</p><a href=\"#0-pick-a-client\" id=\"lnk-0-pick-a-client\">0. Pick a client</a><a href=\"#1-a-token\" id=\"lnk-1-a-token\">1. A token</a><a href=\"#2-the-file-in\" id=\"lnk-2-the-file-in\">2. The file in</a><a href=\"#3-wait-for-the-compile\" id=\"lnk-3-wait-for-the-compile\">3. Wait for the compile</a><a href=\"#4-a-link\" id=\"lnk-4-a-link\">4. A link</a><a href=\"#5-the-numbers-back\" id=\"lnk-5-the-numbers-back\">5. The numbers back</a><a href=\"#6-a-webhook-instead-of-polling\" id=\"lnk-6-a-webhook-instead-of-polling\">6. A webhook instead of polling</a><a href=\"#7-errors\" id=\"lnk-7-errors\">7. Errors</a><a href=\"#the-same-five-calls-elsewhere\" id=\"lnk-the-same-five-calls-elsewhere\">The same five calls, elsewhere</a></aside></section>"}